mapping "VA-VE.1" source="VA-VE" target="d2" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
 confidence 2 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
 comment "en" """
 Source VA-VE = the KSI chapter header for ALL
 activities regarding behaviors and habits (an organizational grouping title spanning VA1 general
 behaviors, VA2 substance/gambling behaviors, and the per-substance VAA/VAB/. children). Target
 ICF d2 (General tasks and demands) is the ICF chapter that
 contains d298A (Handling one's behavior), the corpus's established
 behavior anchor (precedent: SDK -> d298A). Why this target: VA-VE has a coherent topic (unlike
 the WA-WZ residual header mapped to no_match), so a chapter-to-chapter link to d2 is the most
 defensible single anchor; no single ICF code covers the whole VA-VE scope. Why broader (weak):
 weak tier — the link is a coarse chapter-to-chapter mapping where d2 subsumes the behavior/habit
 axis but VA-VE also implicitly spans d230 (routines/habits) and d570 (health behavior); the
 subsumption is real but loose. Athena-local ICF mirror; no web.
 """ suspect=quoted-text
}
